<title>UK: Algeria sets August LPG price at $175 a tonne.</title>
<headline>Algeria sets August LPG price at $175 a tonne.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algerian state oil and gas company Sonatrach  has set its official posted prices for Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG)  for August.</p>
<p>Propane and butane will both be priced at $175 a tonne fob Bethioua.  The premium for loading at Arzew or Skikda will be $5 a tonne.</p>
<p>The propane price is up $8 a tonne from July, while butane is unchanged.  Levels are effective from August 1.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
